From: hayaksi1 <193020925+hayaksi1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 21:02:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Close leaked dialogs between the RoomView cases
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A stepping case dispatches a view of an event the timeline cannot load,
and the resulting error dialog opens asynchronously — often after the case
that provoked it has already ended. Dialogs mount into their own container
outside the render tree, so the library's cleanup never reaches them, and
the focus trap on the survivor then holds document.activeElement through
whichever case runs next. That is what made the caret assertion fail only
when the file ran as a whole.

Closing them has to be flushed rather than merely called: the close path
kicks off a re-render it does not await, and letting that land wherever it
likes made a different handful of stepping cases fail on each run. Driving
it through act settles the teardown before the next case starts, which is
what makes this deterministic rather than trading one flake for several.
---
 apps/web/src/components/structures/RoomView.test.tsx | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/apps/web/src/components/structures/RoomView.test.tsx b/apps/web/src/components/structures/RoomView.test.tsx
index 4e07609c7a..0adb8c8493 100644
--- a/apps/web/src/components/structures/RoomView.test.tsx
+++ b/apps/web/src/components/structures/RoomView.test.tsx
@@ -137,7 +137,11 @@ describe("RoomView", () => {
         vi.spyOn(cli, "getCrypto").mockReturnValue(undefined);
     });
 
-    afterEach(() => {
+    afterEach(async () => {
+        await act(async () => {
+            Modal.forceCloseAllModals();
+        });
+
         unmockPlatformPeg();
         vi.clearAllMocks();
 
